# The lane-10 DRIVER's own artifacts (ops/loop/queue_loop.py, 2026-09-05). Same
# class as the worker logs above and deliberately NOT tracked: the JSONL is
# rewritten every cycle by a process that runs for hours, so committing it would
# put the loop and its own operator in a permanent conflict over one file. The
# durable record of what a cycle did is its COMMIT and its LEDGER entry; this
# file is the local flight recorder for the run in progress.
ops/loop/reports/queue_loop.jsonl
ops/loop/reports/queue_loop.log
ops/loop/reports/queue_loop.log.err
